Hrm. One possibility would be that random gems could be enchanted ("You see
here a softly glowing emerald"), but if it would be easier to code new
ones...

a mana crystal/sapphire/emerald/ruby/diamond/etc ("A chunk of congealed
magical essence")

You could add several colors of increasing potency, matching the existing
gem rarities (ie, mana diamonds would be the rarest of already rare mana
gems), giving more of a boost when used for casting, and appearing the same
as other similarly colored gems.

Throwing them could have magical effects (crystal mm, sapphire cold, emerald
poison, ruby fire, diamond cancellation?) - perhaps of a higher potency than
equivalent wands, as they would be one shot

Wielding the gems to release their energy seems uncomfortable, but applying
them or simply consuming them from inventory perhaps. Applying the gem would
release its energy (with no identifiable message "You hold the gem in your
hand for a moment.") - if you cast in the next (n) turns, the gem is
consumed. If un'id'd, this could be potentially fatal, as it would release
the energy at you, should you not use it (or toss it quickly) (discouraging
easy id, though this seems perhaps too easy, but you'd be foolish even in
the midgame with more hp to apply an unidentified white gem...). Could also
randomize the effects among all gem types, making it even more risky (oops,
looks like sapphire was cancellation!)

Could be used with a sling for greater effect/range

Monsters could toss them at you

Eating them (as an appropriate creature) could gain pp and/or health - some
casters might carry a few (late game creatures?). Do creatures actually use
pp?

Dropping/dipping them into water/lava (when of the appropriate type) could
freeze/boil the water/lava.

Dipping them in potions could have appropriate effects. Break, freeze, boil,
sicken, cancel (others?), in addition to releasing the energy on you (as
applied above)

Dipping into fountains, I'm not sure about. Strange effects? Nothing?

Tossing them at a unicorn could have an odd effect... :D (making willy nilly
gem tossing at unicorns a Bad Idea)

Gives a bit more value to Archs. Makes gems more interesting... adds more
potential YASD's from fooling with them. Gives you a bit of extra oomph as a
caster. Another ranged weapon/tool as a melee. More interactions with the
dungeon.

Hmm. Thoughts?



